                <pb facs="0669" n="597" xml:id="pg597"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 21558/3.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Vice and Deputy Consul General Cauldwell to the
                        Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Alexandria</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-10-02"><hi rendition="#italic">October 2,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Egyptian ministry for foreign affairs says it is unable to arrest Memar Rizk, as
                    he is a Syrian, but will arrest him on request of Turkish Government. Meantime
                    Rizk will be searched out and watched.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cauldwell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
